 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-009\",\n \"clauses\": {\"compare\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F04\", \"template\": \"Which is {comp_word}: {val_a} {unit_a} or {val_b} {unit_b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F04 is a question-level comparison of two counts of units, with comp_word drawn from longer/shorter. Its unit domain prints only plural members (crayons, hands, paperclips), so it does not share F01's singular-noun fault.\"}, \"lengths\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F03\", \"template\": \"The {comparison} {measure} is {answer} {count_noun}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F03's measure domain offers the member 'length', the only family that names lengths. F03 is also one of the failing families, for the singular count_noun reason below. The clause is still addressed by the template.\"}, \"distances\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"The distance from the bench to the tree is {val_a} {unit_a}. The distance from the gate to the tree is {val_b} {unit_b}. Which distance is {comp_word}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 prints 'distance' as the measure in two sentences and asks which is longer or shorter. Its unit domain prints only plural members (blocks, hands) for values 2 to 9, so it is clean.\"}, \"non_standard_units\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F04\", \"template\": \"Which is {comp_word}: {val_a} {unit_a} or {val_b} {unit_b}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F04 prints non-standard units (crayons, hands, paperclips) as the counting units for the lengths compared, with values 2 to 9 printed by the value domains.\"}},\n \"failing_families\": [\"F01\", \"F03\"],\n \"failing_templates\": [\"Compare {val_a} {count_noun} and {val_b} {count_noun2}.\", \"The {comparison} {measure} is {answer} {count_noun}.\"],\n \"overall\": \"FAIL\",\n \"reasoning\": \"F01 and F03 take count_noun from the generator's own choices, whose basis is 'the unit word or its singular (dna.base.count_noun)', and the members include the singular forms 'block', 'crayon', 'hand' and 'paperclip' alongside the plurals. The value slots they print with are 'repeats a generated value' with printed_runs '2 to 9', so every value that can appear is 2 or more. The domain's distinct_in_every_render is false, so no check ties the singular noun to a value of 1 (the only count that takes a singular). The domain therefore admits ungrammatical learner text such as a singular noun after a count of 2 to 9, in the hint of F01 and the hint of F03. F02 and F04 print only plural unit members and are not at fault. F05 ('{max} is more than {min}.') and F06 ('{key}') are not at fault on the domains shown. For F02 and F04, the value slots val_a and val_b carry no distinctness flag in the packet; I did not treat equal values as a fault, because F05 declares its two compared values distinct in every render, but that inference is not stated for val_a and val_b. The vocabulary 'distance', 'longer' and 'shorter' is not in cumulative_vocab, and 'distance' appears in this lc's own curriculum_vocab and introduces_vocab through 'compare distances'; I did not treat these as gate violations. Clause verdicts cite the families that best produce each clause, with the templates copied exactly as printed in the packet.\"}",
